// library_exec_foreign_reaches_still_fires.strata -- the "no weakening"
// twin of library_exec_no_foreign_discharges.strata (T-0223). SAME node
// (`runner`, `may "exec"`) and the SAME discharging claim SHAPE (`assert
// "weakness:CWE-78:runner" noflow foreign -> runner`), but this model
// DOES declare a `foreign`-trust node (`caller`) with a real, unendorsed
// flow into `runner`. `_claims.py::_expand` now resolves `foreign` to
// `("caller",)` instead of the empty tuple, so `_eval_noflow`'s witness
// search finds the real `caller -> f_invoke -> runner` path and REFUTES
// the claim -- THREAT003 fires exactly as it would with no claim at all.
//
// Proves the library-mode discharge-by-absence mechanism
// (library_exec_no_foreign_discharges.strata) is sound, not a blanket
// weakening: writing `noflow foreign -> <node>` only discharges when the
// model genuinely has no foreign source reaching the sink; the moment one
// exists with no boundary in the way, the SAME claim is REFUTED and the
// obligation fires, deny-by-default (docs/strata/threat.md#library-mode-
// discharge-by-absence).
//
// tested end to end (parse -> elaborate -> check_discharge_completeness)
// by tests/unit/strata/test_threat.py::TestLibraryModeForeignlessDischarge.

module library_exec_foreign_reaches_still_fires

node caller : foreign { clearance Public; }
node runner : trusted {
    clearance Internal;
    may "exec";
}

flow f_invoke : caller -> runner { label Public; }

assert "weakness:CWE-78:runner" noflow foreign -> runner

// frob:waive REF002 reason="litmus fixture read by exactly one dedicated test module by design (T-0145/T-0255/T-0256/T-0262/T-0172/T-0154/T-0155/T-0223/T-0226 litmus suites); a second consumer would not be genuine"
